# Shell scripts run inside Linux containers (postgres-local, redis-tls, worker, fhirbridge-app
# entrypoints; containerization/scripts/*.sh) - CRLF line endings break their shebang line
# (`#!/usr/bin/env bash` becomes `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` once checked out with CRLF, which fails at
# container startup with `env: can't execute 'bash ': No such file or directory`, exit code 127).
# This is silent until it happens: the repo had no .gitattributes at all before this, so whether a
# given clone got LF or CRLF depended entirely on that machine's own `core.autocrlf` setting -
# confirmed live when an image built on such a machine crash-looped with exactly that error, despite
# every script being LF in other working copies (including this one). Force LF unconditionally,
# regardless of the checking-out machine's own git config, so this can't recur.
*.sh text eol=lf
